Architecture-dependent reference behaviour. to-int converts a float64
context number with Go's int(f), which is implementation-defined when f is
out of range: amd64 gives math.MinInt64, arm64 saturates. Endorsers on
different architectures rendered different text. Goldens are kept per
GOARCH (golden/float-to-int.arch.<goarch>.json); an architecture without
a golden file is not checked.
-- to-int.hbs --
{{to-int a}}
-- to-int.jsonl --
{"a":1e21}
{"a":-1e21}
{"a":9223372036854775807}
{"a":1e300}
-- to-str-to-int.hbs --
{{to-str (to-int a)}}
-- to-str-to-int.jsonl --
{"a":1e21}
-- date-add-months-overflow.hbs --
{{date-add-months "2020-01-01" (to-int a)}}
-- date-add-months-overflow.jsonl --
{"a":1e21}
